140 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 112 0 R
/E (An analysis based on PISA \(Programme for International Student Assessment\) data showed that Brazil ranked 17th out of 20 countries evaluated in financial literacy, highlighting the need to expand access to financial education for young people. The study also revealed that 89.8% of young Brazilians learn about money primarily at home, while only a portion receive adequate financial guidance at school. Furthermore, research with Brazilian students indicates that many young people have limited knowledge of financial planning, investments, and expense control, demonstrating insecurity in managing their own money. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
141 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 112 0 R
/E (Conclusion These data reinforce the importance of platforms like EduFinance, which seeks to democratize access to financial education through technology, practical simulations, and accessible content for young investors.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
